For setting up EKS Cluster:
https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/automode.html

For Setting up Load Balancer:

https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/auto-elb-example.html

# Guide for setting up an ALB Ingress Controller on EKS

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: aircraft-maintenance
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: aircraft-maintenance
  ports:
    - port: 8000
      targetPort: 8000

---
apiVersion: eks.amazonaws.com/v1
kind: IngressClassParams
metadata:
  name: alb
spec:
  scheme: internet-facing

---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: IngressClass
metadata:
  name: alb
spec:
  controller: eks.amazonaws.com/alb
  parameters:
    apiGroup: eks.amazonaws.com
    kind: IngressClassParams
    name: alb

---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: aircraft-maintenance
spec:
  ingressClassName: alb
  rules:
    - http:
        paths:
          - path: /
            pathType: Prefix
            backend:
              service:
                name: aircraft-maintenance
                port:
                  number: 8000

Then check:

kubectl get ingress
kubectl describe ingress aircraft-maintenance
kubectl get ingress aircraft-maintenance \
  -o jsonpath='{.status.loadBalancer.ingress[0].hostname}'


Also verify the current state:

kubectl get svc -A
kubectl get ingressclass
kubectl get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp

